  "notes": "Source: Bais Medrash Mayan Hatorah Student Catalog 2025-2026 (official PDF), 'Sample Curriculum' section; hand-transcribed 2026-10-01. Catalog Degree Requirements: 'An Associate of Talmudic Studies Degree is earned upon the completion of 60 credits' with a minimum 2.0 cumulative GPA; 'There is only one major available, Talmud.' Credit reconciliation: 5 terms x 12 credits (5+4+2+1 per term) = 60, exactly the catalog's 60-credit requirement. Course codes are the catalog's own: '**' is the tractate number (01-12) per the catalog's tractate list (Succah, Megillah, Gittin, Kiddushin, Baba Kama, Baba Metzia, Makkos, Baba Basra, Brachos, Pesachim, Beitza, Taanis); the tractate studied varies by year of entry (catalog: 'students entering the institution at different years will study four tractates over the course of their four-year program'). The catalog's course-description heading prints Intermediate Ethics as E2101 (duplicating Beginning Ethics); the Sample Curriculum uses E3101 - the seed follows the Sample Curriculum (beyond this plan's scope; documented for the record). No formal prerequisites are stated in the catalog; prereq arrays are empty (year-level progression is inherent in the published sequence, not invented). The catalog's optional additional 1-credit Talmud Survey elective is not part of the Sample Curriculum and is excluded (including it would break the 60-credit sum). The Bachelor of Talmudic Studies was REFUSED: the catalog's full Sample Curriculum sums to 132 credits (11 terms x 12) versus its stated 120-credit requirement - internally inconsistent with no honest fix; details in scratch/.",
